Environment Variables
New .env.example additions:


# Database (Required for Phase 2)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@db.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# NextAuth.js (Required for Phase 2)
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=your_nextauth_secret_minimum_32_characters

# Base URL for OAuth callbacks
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# GitHub OAuth App Credentials
# Create at: https://github.com/settings/developers
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your_github_oauth_client_id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your_github_oauth_client_secret

# Token Encryption Key (Required for Phase 2)
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_64_character_hex_encryption_key
Implementation Steps (Sequential)
Week 1: Database & Encryption Foundation

Create Supabase project and get DATABASE_URL
Install dependencies: npm install prisma @prisma/client next-auth@beta @auth/prisma-adapter
Create prisma/schema.prisma with User/Account/Session/VerificationToken models
Run initial migration: npx prisma migrate dev --name init
Generate Prisma client: npx prisma generate
Create lib/db/prisma.ts (singleton pattern)
Create lib/auth/encryption.ts (AES-256-GCM encrypt/decrypt functions)
Test database connection: npx prisma studio
Week 2: GitHub OAuth Integration
9. Create GitHub OAuth App at https://github.com/settings/developers

Homepage URL: http://localhost:3000
Callback URL: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/github
Scopes: read:user user:email repo
Add OAuth credentials to .env.local
Create lib/auth/index.ts (NextAuth.js configuration)
Create app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts (export handlers)
Create types/next-auth.d.ts (TypeScript type augmentation)
Create components/auth/AuthProvider.tsx (SessionProvider wrapper)
Create components/auth/SignInButton.tsx (OAuth trigger)
Create components/auth/UserMenu.tsx (user profile dropdown)
Update app/layout.tsx to wrap app with AuthProvider and add nav
Test OAuth flow end-to-end
Week 3: Per-User GitHub Access
19. Create lib/auth/github-client.ts (factory function for authenticated Octokit)
20. Modify lib/github.ts:
- Remove global octokit constant
- Add optional octokit?: Octokit parameter to all functions:
- getRepoInfo(owner, repo, octokit?)
- getRepoFileTree(owner, repo, maxDepth, octokit?)
- getFileContent(owner, repo, path, octokit?)
- getMultipleFileContents(owner, repo, paths, octokit?)
- Create default factory: getDefaultOctokit()
21. Modify app/api/analyze/route.ts:
- Import getAuthenticatedOctokit() from lib/auth/github-client
- Call await getAuthenticatedOctokit() to get user's Octokit client
- Pass client to all GitHub API functions
- Add fallback to shared token for anonymous users
22. Update app/analyze/page.tsx to show "Sign in to analyze private repos" CTA
23. Test private repository analysis with authenticated user

Backward Compatibility
Anonymous users can still analyze public repositories (uses shared GITHUB_TOKEN or no token)
No breaking changes to existing AnalysisResult type or API contract
All GitHub API wrapper functions remain backward compatible with default parameters
Clear CTAs guide users to sign in for private repo access
Security Considerations
Token Storage: GitHub access tokens encrypted with AES-256-GCM before database storage
Encryption Key: 32-byte key stored in TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY environment variable (never in code)
Session Security: Database sessions with 30-day expiration (NextAuth.js default)
CSRF Protection: Built into NextAuth.js
OAuth Scopes: Minimal required scopes (read:user user:email repo)
No Token Exposure: Tokens never returned in API responses or exposed to client
Phase 2.2: User Analysis History
Overview
Store analysis results for authenticated users and provide a history UI to revisit past analyses.

Database Schema Extension
Add to prisma/schema.prisma:


model User {
  // ... existing fields ...
  analyses      Analysis[]  // Add this relation
}

model Analysis {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId    String

  // Repository information
  repoUrl      String
  repoOwner    String
  repoName     String
  repoFullName String  // e.g., "vercel/next.js"

  // Analysis result (stored as JSONB for flexibility)
  result       Json

  // Metadata
  analyzedFiles Int
  totalFiles    Int
  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())

  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@index([userId, createdAt(sort: Desc)])
  @@index([repoFullName])
}
