Summary
This plan provides a production-ready roadmap for Phase 2 implementation with:

✅ Clear separation into two sequential stages

Phase 2.1: OAuth + Private Repos (Weeks 1-3)
Phase 2.2: Analysis History (Weeks 4-5)
✅ Production-grade technology choices

Prisma + Supabase for type-safe persistence
NextAuth.js v5 for OAuth and session management
AES-256-GCM encryption for token security
✅ Backward compatibility maintained

Anonymous users can still analyze public repos
No breaking changes to existing APIs
Graceful degradation without authentication
✅ Security best practices

Encrypted token storage
Database sessions
Minimal OAuth scopes
CSRF protection
✅ Quality standards for Big Tech recruiters

Type safety throughout
Clean architecture with separation of concerns
Comprehensive verification strategy
Production-ready error handling
This phased approach allows for testing and validation at each stage while delivering immediate value with OAuth authentication before adding the convenience of analysis history.